{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlswing"]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLSwingV","title":"MXLSwing","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLSwing","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSwing"}]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"The swing element specifies whether or not to use swing playback, where consecutive on-beat \/ off-beat eighth","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or 16th notes are played with unequal nominal durations.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSwing\/init(content:style:)"],"anchor":"Initializers"},{"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSwing\/content-swift.property","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSwing\/style"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"title":"Enumerations","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSwing\/Content-swift.enum","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSwing\/Kind"],"anchor":"Enumerations"},{"title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSwing\/Equatable-Implementations"],"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSwing"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSwing","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The straight element specifies that no swing is present, so consecutive notes have equal durations.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The first and second elements are positive integers that specify the ratio between durations of consecutive","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"notes. For example, a first element with a value of 2 and a second element with a value of 1 applied to eighth","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"notes specifies a quarter note \/ eighth note tuplet playback, where the first note is twice as long as the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"second note. Ratios should be specified with the smallest integers possible. For example, a ratio of 6 to 4","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"should be specified as 3 to 2 instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The optional swing-type element specifies the note type, either eighth or 16th, to which the ratio is applied.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The value is eighth if this element is not present.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The optional swing-style element is a string describing the style of swing used.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The swing element has no effect for playback of grace notes, notes where a type element is not present, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"notes where the specified duration is different than the nominal value associated with the specified type. If","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a swung note has attack and release attributes, those values modify the swung playback.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<swing>"},{"text":" element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"]]},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/SH":{"title":"Swift.Hashable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSwing":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlswing","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSwing","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSwing"}],"title":"MXLSwing","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The swing element specifies whether or not to use swing playback, where consecutive on-beat \/ off-beat eighth"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or 16th notes are played with unequal nominal durations."}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSwing"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/s8CopyableP":{"title":"Swift.Copyable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSwing/Content-swift.enum":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlswing\/content-swift.enum","title":"MXLSwing.Content","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Content"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"One of the alternatives for Swing."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSwing\/Content-swift.enum"},"doc://IvorMXL/SQ":{"title":"Swift.Equatable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ"},"doc://IvorMXL/s8SendableP":{"title":"Swift.Sendable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP"},"doc://IvorMXL/documenta